{
  "number": 1644,
  "title": "[BUG] ValueError raised when resuming execution with interruptResponse: _convert_prompt_to_messages validation fails",
  "url": "https://github.com/strands-agents/harness-sdk/issues/1644",
  "state": "closed",
  "created_at": "2026-02-06T12:10:32Z",
  "closed_at": "2026-06-19T16:17:38Z",
  "body": "### Checks\n\n- [x] I have updated to the lastest minor and patch version of Strands\n- [x] I have checked the documentation and this is not expected behavior\n- [x] I have searched [./issues](./issues?q=) and there are no duplicates of my issue\n\n### Strands Version\n\n1.23.0\n\n### Python Version\n\n3.12\n\n### Operating System\n\nAmazon Linux 2023\n\n### Installation Method\n\npip\n\n### Steps to Reproduce\n\n1. Define an agent with a tool that triggers an interrupt (e.g., dataops-approval).\n2. Run the agent and catch the interrupt.\n3. Construct the interruptResponse payload.\n4. Call the agent/server again with the response payload.\n\n```\n# ... agent setup ...\n\n# Initial call\nresult = server(json.dumps(payload))\n\nwhile True:\n    if result.stop_reason != \"interrupt\":\n        break\n\n    responses = []\n    for interrupt in result.interrupts:\n        # Constructing the response as per docs\n        if interrupt.name == \"dataops-approval\":\n            responses.append({\n                \"interruptResponse\": {\n                    \"interruptId\": interrupt.id, \n                    \"response\": \"n\"\n                }\n            })\n    \n    # This call triggers the error\n    result = server(responses)\n```\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nThe agent should accept the interruptResponse payload (list of dicts) to resume execution, bypassing the prompt text conversion logic, or the validator should be updated to accept interruptResponse structures.\n\n### Actual Behavior\n\nFile \"/.../site-packages/strands/agent/agent.py\", line 790, in _convert_prompt_to_messages\n    raise ValueError(\"Input prompt must be of type: `str | list[Contentblock] | Messages | None`.\")\nValueError: Input prompt must be of type: `str | list[Contentblock] | Messages | None`.\n\n### Additional Context\n\nI checked the source code for version 1.23.0. The method _convert_prompt_to_messages (referenced in the traceback) validates the input prompt argument:\n\n[https://github.com/strands-agents/sdk-python/blob/f87925b9383a8ead59f0138e55e8412478c70928/src/strands/agent/agent.py#L747-L790](https://www.google.com/search?q=https://github.com/strands-agents/sdk-python/blob/f87925b9383a8ead59f0138e55e8412478c70928/src/strands/agent/agent.py%23L747-L790)\n\nIt strictly checks if the input is str, list[ContentBlock], or Messages. When passing a list of dictionaries (the interrupt responses), this validation fails. It seems the logic does not verify if the input is an interruptResponse payload before attempting to convert it as a standard prompt.\n\n### Possible Solution\n\n_No response_\n\n### Related Issues\n\n_No response_",
